WEBVTT

00:01:33.260 --> 00:01:34.970
I'm home.

00:01:34.970 --> 00:01:37.390
Not like there's anyone else here.

00:01:48.390 --> 00:01:50.680
It worked!

00:01:50.680 --> 00:01:52.680
I knew the Grand Magus could do it!

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:55.680
Are you all right?

00:02:06.010 --> 00:02:08.300
T'would seem the ritual
was a grand success!

00:02:25.590 --> 00:02:27.970
It is my great honor to meet you.

00:02:27.970 --> 00:02:29.930
You must be our Saint.

00:02:31.680 --> 00:02:33.140
What?

00:02:33.800 --> 00:02:36.680
This is the Kingdom of Salutania.

00:02:36.680 --> 00:02:42.180
Since ancient times, the Kingdom
has lived within a shroud of miasma,

00:02:42.180 --> 00:02:46.220
which, when heavy and thick, warps
the bodies and minds of living creatures,

00:02:46.220 --> 00:02:49.930
bringing forth terrible monsters
that ravage the world.

00:02:49.930 --> 00:02:55.140
While the Kingdom's Orders of Knights
fight tooth and nail to protect us all,

00:02:55.140 --> 00:03:01.470
there are periods when the miasma grows
too thick to keep the beasts at bay.

00:03:01.470 --> 00:03:07.090
During those periods, a holy maiden
called the "Saint" will appear.

00:03:07.090 --> 00:03:09.800
The Saint will use her power
to obliterate the monsters,

00:03:09.800 --> 00:03:12.840
and some say her mere presence
lifts the weight of the miasma.

00:03:12.840 --> 00:03:15.180
Her power and grace
keeps the Kingdom at peace

00:03:15.180 --> 00:03:19.260
and shines as a light of hope for
the citizens that live within Her borders.

00:03:19.260 --> 00:03:22.390
Or so it is written in our ancient texts.

00:03:23.550 --> 00:03:25.430
You must be our Saint.

00:03:26.510 --> 00:03:28.390
However, in dire times,
when a Saint did not appear,

00:03:28.390 --> 00:03:30.890
the Kingdom's sages devised
a Saint-summoning ritual,

00:03:30.890 --> 00:03:34.470
one that would call forth a woman
with the Saint's divine powers--

00:03:34.470 --> 00:03:41.010
Th-The miasma must be especially bad
if <i>two</i> Saints were summoned!

00:03:41.010 --> 00:03:42.720
That's my hypothesis, anyway...

00:03:43.720 --> 00:03:47.640
So, how do I go back?

00:03:47.640 --> 00:03:50.890
A-About that, well...

00:03:52.640 --> 00:03:55.050
Please wait, Holy Saint!

00:04:03.010 --> 00:04:05.050
May I ask where you're going, Holy Saint?

00:04:05.050 --> 00:04:06.890
I'm leaving.

00:04:08.220 --> 00:04:10.090
As is your divine right.

00:04:10.090 --> 00:04:16.930
If you truly wish to leave,
then it would be improper to stop you.

00:04:16.930 --> 00:04:22.510
But would you do us the honor of lending
us your ear for a few more moments more?

00:04:32.550 --> 00:04:37.550
...and that would be our Kingdom's
current state of affairs.

00:04:37.550 --> 00:04:42.340
Know that we are appalled by
Prince Kyle's rude behavior towards you.

00:04:42.340 --> 00:04:45.180
Please accept my most humble apologies.

00:04:45.180 --> 00:04:49.430
Unfortunately, I would not think it wise
to live outside the walls of the Palace.

00:04:49.430 --> 00:04:54.590
It is simply not safe
for someone of your stature.

00:04:56.140 --> 00:04:59.430
Oh. Okay.

00:04:59.430 --> 00:05:05.090
I guess I'll have to spend some time
getting used to living in this world.

00:05:05.090 --> 00:05:07.510
If you'd like, Holy Saint,

00:05:07.510 --> 00:05:13.390
you are more than welcome to
make your lodgings here in the Palace.

00:05:14.800 --> 00:05:16.550
Okay.

00:05:17.970 --> 00:05:19.930
But...

00:05:19.930 --> 00:05:23.970
Could you please stop
calling me Holy Saint?

00:05:34.840 --> 00:05:39.470
Ugh. There's nothing to do.

00:05:39.470 --> 00:05:43.840
No one's come to talk to me since.
Are they doing this on purpose?

00:05:43.840 --> 00:05:46.090
Sure, the maid's taking care of me,

00:05:46.090 --> 00:05:49.510
but I can't spend every
waking moment talking to her.

00:05:50.180 --> 00:05:52.720
No TV, no phone, just one room...

00:05:52.720 --> 00:05:56.220
At the very least, I'm a lot more relaxed.

00:05:57.550 --> 00:06:02.220
Would it be all right
if I went for a little walk?

00:06:02.220 --> 00:06:05.390
Of course. Let me call for an escort.

00:06:05.390 --> 00:06:09.090
Oh, no, thanks,
I-I'll be fine! Promise.

00:06:09.090 --> 00:06:11.930
I'm just going to go into
the garden, that's all.

00:06:11.930 --> 00:06:15.340
Are you quite sure? Very well, then.

00:06:25.220 --> 00:06:28.090
I feel a little guilty, but oh, well...

00:06:29.090 --> 00:06:32.220
It's nice to get a little time alone.

00:06:54.720 --> 00:06:56.720
Lavender!

00:07:00.140 --> 00:07:03.590
It smells the same, too. So calming.

00:07:04.640 --> 00:07:08.640
I wonder if the plants in this
world are the same, too.

00:07:08.640 --> 00:07:09.720
Hello, there.

00:07:13.390 --> 00:07:15.640
Can I help you?

00:07:15.640 --> 00:07:17.430
Oh, I'm sorry!

00:07:17.430 --> 00:07:20.550
I was just passing by and got distracted
by these wonderful herbs.

00:07:20.550 --> 00:07:21.890
Wonderful?

00:07:23.390 --> 00:07:27.180
I'm glad to hear that.
Please, look all you like.

00:07:28.470 --> 00:07:31.550
Are the plants in this garden
just for show?

00:07:31.550 --> 00:07:34.090
Just for show? Oh, no.

00:07:34.090 --> 00:07:38.590
These medicinal herbs are used
to craft potions for research.

00:07:38.590 --> 00:07:40.590
P-Potions?

00:07:40.590 --> 00:07:44.090
Yeah! Angelica, rosemary...

00:07:44.090 --> 00:07:46.390
Each plant produces
its own potent effects,

00:07:46.390 --> 00:07:50.140
from relieving fatigue
to inducing sleep.

00:07:50.140 --> 00:07:53.680
We can make use of these effects
by drying or boiling them,

00:07:53.680 --> 00:07:57.510
but those effects are further amplified
when they're mixed into a potion.

00:07:57.510 --> 00:08:01.050
O-Oh, wow, that's incredible.

00:08:01.050 --> 00:08:05.140
Potions? I thought those
only existed in video games.

00:08:05.140 --> 00:08:07.010
You're quite the expert.

00:08:07.010 --> 00:08:09.140
Well, it <i>is</i> my job.

00:08:09.140 --> 00:08:10.390
Your job?

00:08:10.390 --> 00:08:13.390
Yes, I work just down the way
at the Research Institute.

00:08:13.390 --> 00:08:17.970
There, we research herbs and potions
to study their properties and effects.

00:08:19.550 --> 00:08:21.260
A Research Institute...

00:08:21.260 --> 00:08:23.840
Would you like to visit the Institute?

00:08:23.840 --> 00:08:25.590
Could I?!

00:08:52.800 --> 00:08:55.510
Thank you so much for the tour today.

00:08:55.510 --> 00:08:58.840
I had so much fun
talking with you, Ser Jude.

00:08:58.840 --> 00:09:01.010
Please, just Jude is fine.

00:09:01.010 --> 00:09:05.470
I enjoyed our time, too, especially
since you know so much about herbs.

00:09:05.470 --> 00:09:07.640
I hope you'll stop by again soon.

00:09:22.840 --> 00:09:27.220
You certainly seem to be
in good spirits today.

00:09:27.220 --> 00:09:29.300
Y-You think so?

00:09:29.300 --> 00:09:30.340
I do.

00:09:30.340 --> 00:09:33.140
I've seen many more smiles
on your face these past few days

00:09:33.140 --> 00:09:37.050
than I did at the start
of my time with you.

00:09:37.050 --> 00:09:39.800
Where are your walks
taking you these days?

00:09:39.800 --> 00:09:42.510
The Medicinal Flora Research Institute.

00:09:42.510 --> 00:09:46.470
I was really into plants and medicinal
herbs back when I lived in my world.

00:09:46.470 --> 00:09:48.510
Is that so?

00:09:48.510 --> 00:09:52.550
But the Research Institute is
quite a ways from here, is it not?

00:09:52.550 --> 00:09:55.510
Oh, uh...

00:09:55.510 --> 00:09:58.260
She's got a point. It's pretty far.

00:09:58.260 --> 00:10:00.720
Y-You <i>live</i> there?!

00:10:00.720 --> 00:10:05.800
Yes. We're a fair distance from the
palace, and even further from the Capital.

00:10:05.800 --> 00:10:08.640
A good handful of us prefer
to live here at the Institute.

00:10:08.640 --> 00:10:10.300
Wow.

00:10:11.640 --> 00:10:14.470
Hey there, Miss Sei. Good to see you.

00:10:14.470 --> 00:10:17.090
Oh, hello. Thank you
for letting me visit again.

00:10:17.090 --> 00:10:19.590
You're welcome to visit anytime.

00:10:19.590 --> 00:10:24.760
Ser Director, Miss Sei would like
to live here at the Institute, too.

00:10:24.760 --> 00:10:28.680
Is that so? Would you like to
officially become a researcher?

00:10:30.550 --> 00:10:33.590
I-If that's allowed,
then yeah, absolutely.

00:10:33.590 --> 00:10:37.300
But it can't be <i>that</i> easy
to become a researcher, can it?

00:10:37.300 --> 00:10:41.930
Still, if I'm going to keep
coming here to stay busy,

00:10:41.930 --> 00:10:44.800
I might as well make it official.

00:10:44.800 --> 00:10:48.890
It's better than sitting around
bored all the time, anyway.

00:10:50.840 --> 00:10:53.640
Yes, I do.

00:10:53.640 --> 00:10:55.760
I want to be a researcher!

00:10:57.470 --> 00:11:01.890
Very well, then.
I'll get the formalities sorted.

00:11:04.720 --> 00:11:07.050
Well, no time to waste!

00:11:07.050 --> 00:11:09.390
I'll see you later!

00:11:13.010 --> 00:11:14.470
Miss Marie!

00:11:17.470 --> 00:11:18.890
That's quite all right.

00:11:18.890 --> 00:11:20.640
Wait, really?

00:11:20.640 --> 00:11:21.680
Of course.

00:11:21.680 --> 00:11:27.840
A member of the Institute just stopped by
to speak with us about it, in fact.

00:11:27.840 --> 00:11:30.180
Wow, they work fast.

00:11:30.180 --> 00:11:31.720
I believe I speak for all of us,

00:11:31.720 --> 00:11:37.430
but after causing you so much trouble,
we're glad to provide whatever we can.

00:11:37.430 --> 00:11:40.010
I-I really appreciate that!

00:11:42.590 --> 00:11:43.640
Here you are.

00:11:43.640 --> 00:11:48.550
All of the belongings you had upon you
when you arrived are within that case.

00:11:48.550 --> 00:11:53.680
The rest of your effects have already
been transported to the Institute.

00:11:53.680 --> 00:11:56.260
Thank you so much for everything.

00:11:56.260 --> 00:12:00.800
If you ever need anything,
please don't hesitate to reach out.

00:12:00.800 --> 00:12:02.800
I will, thank you!

00:12:02.800 --> 00:12:04.800
Save travels to you!

00:12:20.140 --> 00:12:23.720
My name is Sei. I'll be joining you
at the Institute from here on out.

00:12:23.720 --> 00:12:25.510
It's very nice to meet you all!

00:12:25.510 --> 00:12:28.840
Right then, who should
take charge of you...

00:12:28.840 --> 00:12:30.640
Jude, she's all yours.

00:12:30.640 --> 00:12:32.260
Wait, me?

00:12:32.260 --> 00:12:34.930
You're the one who brought her
into this mess, right?

00:12:34.930 --> 00:12:38.010
I-It's nice to be working with you, Jude.

00:12:38.010 --> 00:12:40.260
Yeah, same here.

00:12:46.550 --> 00:12:49.720
Right, then! First, let me explain
what it is we do here.

00:12:49.720 --> 00:12:50.550
Okay.

00:12:50.550 --> 00:12:55.090
Our Institute focuses
primarily on medicinal herbs.

00:12:55.090 --> 00:12:57.930
That, and the potions that
make use of their effects.

00:12:57.930 --> 00:12:59.930
This, here, is a potion.

00:12:59.930 --> 00:13:04.430
You can use it for most anything, like
regenerating wounds or as an antidote,

00:13:04.430 --> 00:13:07.090
and it can be ingested orally or applied
externally during first aid.

00:13:07.090 --> 00:13:08.430
Wow.

00:13:08.430 --> 00:13:10.680
How about we try making one, huh?

00:13:10.680 --> 00:13:12.390
Yes, please!

00:13:12.390 --> 00:13:15.140
First, we fill a pot with water...

00:13:17.220 --> 00:13:19.300
...and bring that to a light boil.

00:13:21.050 --> 00:13:24.510
Then, we add herbs to the water.

00:13:28.390 --> 00:13:33.260
Once that's heated up just right,
we imbue it with magic power...

00:13:33.260 --> 00:13:36.300
How do you imbue something
with magic power?

00:13:38.300 --> 00:13:39.340
Huh?

00:13:39.590 --> 00:13:40.930
Huh?

00:13:40.930 --> 00:13:45.390
Wait... you've never used magic before?

00:13:45.390 --> 00:13:46.720
Never.

00:13:46.720 --> 00:13:48.680
Not even everyday cantrips?

00:13:48.680 --> 00:13:49.800
Nope.

00:13:51.340 --> 00:13:55.220
A-All right, then.
Let me show you how it's done.

00:13:55.220 --> 00:13:56.510
Okay.

00:14:05.680 --> 00:14:07.340
There! One potion.

00:14:08.430 --> 00:14:11.680
I can only make
low-grade potions for now.

00:14:11.680 --> 00:14:16.390
Still, you can use magic!
That's incredible in itself!

00:14:16.390 --> 00:14:18.840
Y-You think so?

00:14:18.840 --> 00:14:22.720
In any case, you should start off
by learning to cast magic yourself.

00:14:22.720 --> 00:14:24.090
Lend me your hands.

00:14:29.050 --> 00:14:34.090
I'm going to channel some of my magic
power to you. Focus on the sensation.

00:14:35.390 --> 00:14:37.300
Okay, here it comes.

00:14:45.180 --> 00:14:46.890
I feel...

00:14:46.890 --> 00:14:50.180
...something circulating through my body.

00:14:50.180 --> 00:14:52.140
That's it! That's the flow of magic power!

00:14:52.140 --> 00:14:54.970
I can't believe you felt that.
You've got a knack for this!

00:14:54.970 --> 00:14:58.800
Oh, it's only because you're
such a good teacher, Jude.

00:14:58.800 --> 00:15:02.340
Right, let's get you started
making your own potion!

00:15:02.340 --> 00:15:04.340
Sh-Shouldn't I study some more first?!

00:15:04.340 --> 00:15:08.760
No, you'll be fine. It won't explode
or anything if you mess up.

00:15:08.760 --> 00:15:10.840
Are you sure?

00:15:17.140 --> 00:15:22.180
Just imagine that flow from
before pouring into the pot...

00:15:27.470 --> 00:15:29.300
Hold on.

00:15:29.300 --> 00:15:33.390
How much magic power
am I supposed to add?

00:15:33.390 --> 00:15:37.800
Oh, jeez... Is this enough?

00:15:37.800 --> 00:15:39.550
Or should I keep going?

00:15:41.050 --> 00:15:42.340
That's plenty, Sei.

00:15:42.340 --> 00:15:44.470
S-Ser Director!

00:15:44.470 --> 00:15:46.760
Yes. Wonderfully done.

00:15:46.760 --> 00:15:49.970
All you have to do now is let it cool,
then put it into a vial.

00:15:49.970 --> 00:15:52.430
Congratulations on your first potion!

00:16:31.260 --> 00:16:32.140
Come in!

00:16:32.140 --> 00:16:34.390
Sei, may I have a word?

00:16:34.390 --> 00:16:35.800
Of course.

00:16:35.800 --> 00:16:39.180
Is this a potion you crafted, Sei?

00:16:40.680 --> 00:16:42.970
Yes, this is one of mine.

00:16:46.220 --> 00:16:47.890
Fifty percent more effective?

00:16:47.890 --> 00:16:52.890
Yep. All the potions I make
are 1.5 times more effective.

00:16:52.890 --> 00:16:54.800
Did you put something else into them?

00:16:54.800 --> 00:16:58.220
Nope. I only do what you taught me to do.

00:16:59.680 --> 00:17:03.340
It's the same color as any
old low-grade potion.

00:17:03.340 --> 00:17:05.930
Do mid-grade potions
have different colors?

00:17:05.930 --> 00:17:10.090
Yeah. This is a mid-grade potion,

00:17:10.090 --> 00:17:12.340
and this is a high-grade potion.

00:17:12.340 --> 00:17:14.300
Cool!

00:17:14.300 --> 00:17:16.300
Don't get any smart ideas.

00:17:16.300 --> 00:17:19.140
They're really tough to craft.

00:17:19.140 --> 00:17:23.840
Nobody at the Institute can make them,
so we have to order them in.

00:17:23.840 --> 00:17:25.720
Well, look at the bright side!

00:17:25.720 --> 00:17:27.890
Whoever uses that potion
gets a lucky little bonus!

00:17:27.890 --> 00:17:31.470
Fifty percent is too much
to attribute to just "luck"!

00:17:31.470 --> 00:17:34.510
I guess we'll just
have to experiment, then.

00:17:34.510 --> 00:17:37.140
Seeing as this is
a Research Institute and all.

00:17:37.140 --> 00:17:38.180
You're right.

00:17:38.180 --> 00:17:41.470
Ooh, you should show me how to
make mid- and high-grade potions!

00:17:41.470 --> 00:17:43.220
What?! You're not ready!

00:17:43.220 --> 00:17:46.390
C'mon, just show me once, please!

00:18:11.140 --> 00:18:13.760
I can't believe
you can actually craft them.

00:18:13.760 --> 00:18:16.930
Sure, but I still make lots of mistakes.
This is only my third potion.

00:18:16.930 --> 00:18:19.840
Still, you've only been here three months.

00:18:21.260 --> 00:18:25.430
And you keep making piles
upon piles of potions.

00:18:25.430 --> 00:18:29.390
How is it that you never
run out of magic power, Sei?

00:18:29.390 --> 00:18:32.220
So, how many potions
does this make today?

00:18:32.220 --> 00:18:33.800
N-No clue.

00:18:33.800 --> 00:18:36.140
The Director's going to scold you again!

00:18:36.140 --> 00:18:40.430
Your potions are too strong for us
to sell in the civilian marketplace!

00:18:41.720 --> 00:18:44.220
Keep this up, and we'll be out of herbs
to make potions with,

00:18:44.220 --> 00:18:46.140
and that's not to mention our
overflowing storehouses! He's gonna--

00:18:46.140 --> 00:18:47.510
Everyone, we have an emergency!

00:18:47.510 --> 00:18:49.930
Gather up all the healing
potions we have, now!

00:18:54.340 --> 00:18:58.640
A week ago, the Third Order of Knights
ventured into the Western Woods

00:18:58.640 --> 00:19:00.390
to subjugate the growing
population of monsters,

00:19:00.390 --> 00:19:02.260
but they were attacked by a Salamander
and suffered heavy casualties.

00:19:02.260 --> 00:19:05.010
They've just returned to the Royal Palace,
and while none have perished,

00:19:05.010 --> 00:19:08.220
so many are gravely wounded
that they don't have

00:19:08.220 --> 00:19:09.930
enough potions to heal them all.

00:19:11.340 --> 00:19:14.010
We are to gather up all the potions
we have and any supplies we may need

00:19:14.010 --> 00:19:16.720
and head to the Royal Palace
to assist the chirurgeons at once.

00:19:16.720 --> 00:19:18.340
On the double, now!

00:19:28.090 --> 00:19:30.800
So are there dragons
in the Western Woods?

00:19:30.800 --> 00:19:31.890
Dragons?

00:19:31.890 --> 00:19:35.180
A Salamander is a kind
of fire dragon, right?

00:19:35.180 --> 00:19:37.760
No, a Salamander is
a fire-breathing lizard.

00:19:37.760 --> 00:19:40.800
A lizard? One lizard
did <i>that</i> much damage?

00:19:40.800 --> 00:19:43.840
It's much bigger and faster
than the name might suggest.

00:19:43.840 --> 00:19:45.260
It may not be as powerful as a dragon,

00:19:45.260 --> 00:19:48.300
but it's up there with
the more deadly beasts.

00:19:48.300 --> 00:19:50.800
A huge lizard...

00:19:50.800 --> 00:19:52.180
We've arrived.

00:19:56.840 --> 00:19:58.300
This way!

00:20:11.390 --> 00:20:14.300
You there! Get us
those potions, quickly, now!

00:20:14.300 --> 00:20:15.840
Yes, sir!

00:20:19.220 --> 00:20:20.590
Here.

00:20:24.050 --> 00:20:26.470
I feel better now.

00:20:26.470 --> 00:20:27.760
Thank goodness.

00:20:27.760 --> 00:20:30.050
Thank you, kind miss.

00:20:30.970 --> 00:20:34.720
How is it that things are this bad,
and the Saint is nowhere in sight?!

00:20:34.720 --> 00:20:37.140
I hear she can use
high-level healing spells.

00:20:37.140 --> 00:20:38.890
We could really use
a few of those right now...

00:20:38.890 --> 00:20:44.720
Prince Kyle said the Saint was "not to
bear witness to such a horrific scene."

00:20:44.720 --> 00:20:46.470
What?!

00:20:46.470 --> 00:20:48.470
Prince Kyle?

00:20:49.640 --> 00:20:52.470
That means the Saint must be...

00:20:53.760 --> 00:20:57.890
I mean, makes sense.
She might not be able to handle all this.

00:20:57.890 --> 00:20:59.800
Sei!

00:20:59.800 --> 00:21:02.340
Do you have any high-grade potions left?

00:21:02.340 --> 00:21:05.010
Yes, I do!

00:21:05.010 --> 00:21:09.430
Captain! Stay with us, Captain!

00:21:24.590 --> 00:21:26.510
H-Here!

00:21:28.800 --> 00:21:30.840
Please, drink this!

00:21:34.550 --> 00:21:36.010
Drink it!

00:21:39.220 --> 00:21:41.930
Please, you have to drink it!

00:21:49.140 --> 00:21:51.090
Drink, dammit!

00:22:28.640 --> 00:22:29.930
Thank you, miss!

00:22:29.930 --> 00:22:30.660
What an incredible potion!

00:22:30.660 --> 00:22:32.590
You've saved him!

00:22:35.510 --> 00:22:39.260
He's an old friend of mine.

00:22:39.260 --> 00:22:41.260
And you saved his life.

00:22:42.390 --> 00:22:44.760
Thank you, Sei.

00:22:49.140 --> 00:22:49.840
Of course!

00:22:49.970 --> 00:22:52.970
Summoning

00:22:56.470 --> 00:22:57.720
What have you found?

00:22:57.720 --> 00:22:59.720
The exact mechanism is unclear,

00:22:59.720 --> 00:23:03.720
but the potions she crafts
are 50% more effective.

00:23:03.720 --> 00:23:06.720
That's too great a difference
to attribute to mere happenstance.

00:23:06.720 --> 00:23:10.090
And you've checked the materials
and process used to craft them?

00:23:10.090 --> 00:23:10.800
Yes.

00:23:10.800 --> 00:23:14.840
Then could the increased effectiveness
be because she is indeed the Saint?

00:23:14.840 --> 00:23:17.470
It's still too early to determine.

00:23:19.590 --> 00:23:22.430
I see. Have you noticed anything else?

00:23:22.430 --> 00:23:24.260
Not at this time, no.

00:23:24.260 --> 00:23:26.340
I see. Thank you.

00:23:26.340 --> 00:23:28.840
Send word to me if you learn
anything else of importance.

00:23:28.840 --> 00:23:30.800
That will be all.

00:23:30.800 --> 00:23:32.390
Thank you.

00:23:35.010 --> 00:23:40.020
Companionship
